      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1244",
      "html": "<ul><li>pH: 6.0–7.0</li><li>Temperature: 22–27°C</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1244",
      "html": "<p>Females are deeper bodied. Males are more slender and have prominent serrations on the posterior edge of the pectoral spine.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1244",
      "html": "<p>Unreported. There is no breeding report.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1244",
      "html": "<p>Identification: easily distinguished by its distinctive protruding snout and simple barbel morphology.</p><p>Etymology: from the Greek hemi- meaning half and Silurus, the word for catfish. The specific name comes from the Greek heteros- meaning different and rhynchos, meaning snout, in reference to the distinctive snout shape.</p><p>Synonyms: Diastatomycter chaperi, Hemisilurus chaperi, Wallago heterorhynchus.</p><p>IUCN Red List: Least Concern (last assessed 2019).</p>"
    },
